  "correct": "C",
  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Select just the required terms",
      "body": "<p>In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></math>, the coefficient of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"0\"><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00029;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></math>. Find this for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>.</p>",
      "recap": "Targeted binomial extraction avoids expanding terms that cannot contribute.",
      "pitfall": "The powers of both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow></math> change with the selected degree.",
      "pause": "Write the two coefficients without their powers of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l11",
          "reminder": "Targeted binomial extraction avoids expanding terms that cannot contribute."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Apply the coefficient relationship",
      "body": "<p>The coefficients are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>10</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>. The first is eight times the second, so <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>80</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>.</p>",
      "recap": "Translate the stated relationship into an equation before cancelling.",
      "pitfall": "Cancelling <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow></math> is valid because they are positive.",
      "pause": "Simplify the equation and use positivity when taking square roots.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l01",
          "reminder": "Translate the stated relationship into an equation before cancelling."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Use the positive-integer restriction",
      "body": "<p>After cancelling the nonzero factors, use the equation relating the squares to find the positive ratio between the two parameters. Express their sum in terms of one parameter.</p>",
      "recap": "An integer minimum must be attained by allowed integer values.",
      "pitfall": "The value <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> is not permitted.",
      "pause": "Choose the smallest allowed positive integer and its matching parameter, then evaluate their sum.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p2-b3-l06",
          "reminder": "An integer minimum must be attained by allowed integer values."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p>The relevant coefficients are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"0\"><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00029;</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"0\"><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00029;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>. The stated relation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>.</p><p>Since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>, divide by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math> to get <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>16</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>. Positivity selects <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></math>. Therefore <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></math>, whose least possible value occurs at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p>The least sum is <strong>5: C.</strong></p>",
